## Frequently Asked Questions

**Does homeowner's insurance cover tree removal in Ohio?**
If a tree falls and damages a covered structure — your roof, fence, or garage — most policies cover removal of the fallen portion. A tree that falls in your yard without hitting anything is typically not covered. We provide documentation for insurance claims.

**How long does tree removal take?**
Most residential jobs take 2–6 hours. Large trees near structures can take a full day. We give you a time estimate with every quote.

**Do I need a permit to remove a tree in Cleveland?**
It depends on your municipality. Some Cleveland suburbs require permits for trees over a certain size or for street trees. We know the local rules and can flag this during your estimate.

**What's the cheapest time of year to remove a tree in NE Ohio?**
Late fall through winter (November–March) is often when crews have more availability and some companies offer lower rates. That said, we price fairly year-round — call and ask.

**Can you remove a tree the same day?**
For emergencies — tree on a house, blocked driveway, immediate safety risk — yes. We respond 24/7. For standard scheduled removals, we'll set a date that works for you.

